 "note": "Clover: the owner's own black-and-white tuxedo cat: short glossy black coat, white bib narrowing into a belly stripe, white chin and lip spot, white toes, big ears, white whiskers, pale yellow-green eyes that glow in the dark, a glowing four-leaf clover charm on his chest. Egg-only, never spawns naturally.",
 "ability_desc": "Lucky finds: when he's following you on grass or dirt he sometimes stops, sniffs, digs and comes up with a four-leaf clover in his teeth, sets it down and bats your lucky find over to you: gold and iron nuggets, seeds, flowers, now and then an emerald or lapis, rarely a diamond, plus a little Luck (better finds and longer Luck at higher bond). A sleek black-and-white tuxedo cat with a white bib, white chin and white toes, big ears and pale yellow-green eyes that shine in the dark, and 88 clips, 30 of them his own: sits bolt upright with his tail round his toes, gives you the side-eye, washes his white shirt front, swivels his ears like radar, sits on your paperwork (lecterns, bookshelves, cartography tables) and swats things off the page, checks his toes, butt-wiggles and pounces on nothing, claps at bugs, stands up like a meerkat, naps nose-under-tail, meows at doors, rolls in the clover and sniffs flowers until he sneezes. Comes back to you with a gentleman's bow, begs on his hind legs for fish, and crab-hops sideways at creepers. Petting gets a cheek rub, a purring roll or a slow love blink; pet him too much and he nips you, then grooms his shoulder as if nothing happened. Not found in the wild: spawn him with his egg; he arrives already named Clover and is tamed with raw cod.",
